{"article_ids": ["24c1285ad5edaaad"], "canonical_title": "Preview web apps live as your coding agent builds them with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore runtime", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.96, "description": "Amazon Bedrock introduced AgentCore Session endpoints that give each runtime session an authenticated URL. The URL forwards any HTTP method, path, and WebSocket connection to ports you allow. In a demo, a coding agent keeps a Vite website running in its session, and the live site updates in the browser as the agent edits files.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:http", "term:url"], "first_seen": "2026-10-30T21:40:03Z", "id": "evt_24c1285ad5edaaad", "importance_score": 5.39, "last_updated": "2026-10-30T21:40:03Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["e38e6ce4316c7aae", "871d193932e07498", "54f20f9f7f25bd15"], "canonical_title": "From Target Selection to Condition Reuse: Auditing Residual Interventions in Tool-Use Models", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "Drew Breunig released dbreunig/nesformer, a project that encodes a functional Nintendo Entertainment System 6502 CPU emulator directly into the parameters of the Qwen3.5‑4B language model. The emulator can run NES ROMs such as Super Mario Bros inside the model, though at very slow speed. The work builds on the earlier qwenputer project and uses the Opus 5.5 prompt set.", "entities": ["model:qwen", "model:qwen-3.5", "term:nes", "term:risc", "term:url"], "first_seen": "2026-10-26T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_e38e6ce4316c7aae", "importance_score": 5.23, "last_updated": "2026-10-30T21:59:22Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl", "hacker-news", "simon-willison"]}
